          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.784,
      "end": 13.454,
      "text": "Discovered in 1877 by \u00c9douard Stephan, the group in the constellation Pegasus appears to be a tight cluster of five.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Pegasus - Johann Bayer.jpg",
        "credit": "Johann Bayer",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pegasus_-_Johann_Bayer.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 9.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.2,
          "end": 13.467,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.454,
      "end": 21.824,
      "text": "However, modern measurements revealed that its brightest member, NGC 7320, is merely a foreground interloper.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NGC 7320.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, and the Hubble SM4 ERO Team",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NGC_7320.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.467,
          "end": 17.267,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 17.267,
          "end": 21.833,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 21.824,
      "end": 31.194,
      "text": "It sits only thirty-nine million light-years from Earth, while the other four galaxies are parked 210 to 340 million light-years away.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Compass and Scale Image of Stephan's Quintet (2009-25-2583).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, and the Hubble SM4 ERO Team",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Compass_and_Scale_Image_of_Stephan%27s_Quintet_(2009-25-2583).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 21.833,
          "end": 27.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 27.1,
          "end": 31.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.194,
      "end": 42.389,
      "text": "Even wilder, another intruder named NGC 7318B is currently falling into the center at supersonic speeds of several million kilometers per hour.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NGC 7318 taken by James Webb Space Telescope (cropped).png",
        "credit": "Image: \n\nNational Aeronautics and Space Administration  (a U.S. federal government agency; https://www.nasa.gov/)\nEuropean space agency (https://www.esa.int/), Canadian Space Agency (https://www.asc-c",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NGC_7318_taken_by_James_Webb_Space_Telescope_(cropped).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.2,
          "end": 38.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 38.2,
          "end": 42.4,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.389,
      "end": 49.064,
      "text": "This violent impact generates an immense cosmic shock wave bigger than the entire Milky Way.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "X-ray-Optical Mosaic of Stephan's Quintet, Unlabeled (2003-stephan-more-3).tiff",
        "credit": "(Credit: X-ray: NASA/CXC/INAF-Brera/G.Trinchieri et al. Optical: Pal.Obs. DSS)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:X-ray-Optical_Mosaic_of_Stephan%27s_Quintet,_Unlabeled_(2003-stephan-more-3).tiff"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.4,
          "end": 45.1,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 45.1,
          "end": 49.067,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 49.064,
      "end": 53.184,
      "text": "That colossal crash proves the true quintet is still taking shape,",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Stephan\u2019s Quintet (NIRCam + MIRI Imaging) (weic2208a).tiff",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, CSA, and STScI",
